From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: keep the A830 chip id 0x44050000

The upstream node reports 0x44050001. 0x44050000 keeps the Vulkan device
id, and so existing shader caches, unchanged. It is also matched by Mesa
releases before 26.3, which do not know 0x44050001 once the speed-bin
fuse is in the upper bits (older Flatpak runtimes, bundled Mesa builds).

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
@@ -3585,7 +3585,7 @@
 		};
 
 		gpu: gpu@3d00000 {
-			compatible = "qcom,adreno-44050001", "qcom,adreno";
+			compatible = "qcom,adreno-44050000", "qcom,adreno";
 			reg = <0x0 0x03d00000 0x0 0x6d000>,
 			      <0x0 0x03d9e000 0x0 0x2000>;
 			reg-names = "kgsl_3d0_reg_memory",
